---

<DocsLayout
  title="Providers"
  subtitle="How nikcli builds its model catalog, resolves credentials, selects runtime adapters, and streams requests."
  description="Reference for nikcli model providers, credentials, adapters, model filtering, and streaming behavior."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="overview" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      Providers are resolved by <code>packages/nikcli/src/provider/provider.ts</code>. The service
      starts with <code>models.dev</code>, layers local and gateway providers, applies user config
      and saved auth, lets plugins modify providers, filters models, then caches SDK instances and
      model loaders.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-grid not-prose">
      <DocCard title="Catalog" eyebrow="Models">
        <p><code>ModelsDev.get</code> provides the default provider/model database and API package metadata.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Auth" eyebrow="Keys">
        <p>Credentials can come from environment variables, saved auth records, or <code>config.provider.*.options</code>.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="SDK" eyebrow="Adapters">
        <p>Known AI SDK packages are imported directly; unknown provider packages can still be loaded dynamically.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Runtime" eyebrow="Stream">
        <p>Session execution enters <code>session/llm.ts</code>, then uses AI SDK or the native <code>@nikcli-ai/llm</code> runtime when supported.</p>
      </DocCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="resolution" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Provider resolution</h2>
    <p>The provider service constructs the final catalog in this order:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Load <code>models.dev</code> and convert each provider/model into nikcli provider records.</li>
      <li>Apply <code>disabled_providers</code> and <code>enabled_providers</code> filters.</li>
      <li>Probe dynamic local providers such as <code>ollama</code> and <code>nikcli-inference</code>.</li>
      <li>Merge provider overrides from <code>config.provider</code>.</li>
      <li>Merge saved API auth records from <code>Auth.Service</code>.</li>
      <li>Run plugin auth loaders and plugin model loaders.</li>
      <li>Filter alpha, deprecated, unavailable, allow-list, and block-list models.</li>
      <li>Create provider/model caches for SDK instances, language models, and image models.</li>
    </ol>
    <DocCallout type="info" title="Filters are provider-level first">
      <p>
        <code>enabled_providers</code> means only listed providers survive. <code>disabled_providers</code>
        removes providers from automatic loading. Model-level allow/block lists are applied later.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="configure" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Configure a provider</h2>
    <p>
      Provider config is stored under <code>provider</code> in <code>nikcli.json</code>. The schema is
      <code>ModelsDev.Provider.partial</code> plus nikcli options such as API key, base URL, timeout,
      header timeout, chunk timeout, model variants, allow-lists, and block-lists.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="json" title="nikcli.json">
&#123;
  "$schema": "https://nikcli-ai.dev/config.json",
  "model": "openrouter/openai/gpt-5",
  "small_model": "openai/gpt-5-mini",
  "provider": &#123;
    "openrouter": &#123;
      "options": &#123;
        "apiKey": "&#123;env:OPENROUTER_API_KEY&#125;",
        "baseURL": "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1",
        "timeout": 300000,
        "headerTimeout": 10000,
        "chunkTimeout": 60000
      &#125;
    &#125;,
    "ollama": &#123;
      "options": &#123;
        "baseURL": "http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1",
        "apiKey": "ollama"
      &#125;
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;
    </DocCode>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>options.apiKey</code></td><td>Explicit key used when no saved auth or provider-specific env key wins first.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>options.baseURL</code></td><td>OpenAI-compatible or gateway URL, normalized by provider-specific loaders when needed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>options.timeout</code></td><td>Total request timeout in milliseconds, or <code>false</code> to disable.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>options.headerTimeout</code></td><td>Maximum wait for response headers. OpenAI defaults to a configured provider value.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>options.chunkTimeout</code></td><td>Maximum gap between SSE chunks before aborting a stream.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>whitelist</code></td><td>Only keep matching model ids for this provider.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>blacklist</code></td><td>Remove matching model ids for this provider.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>models.*.variants</code></td><td>Variant-level config, including disabled variants.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="bundled" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Bundled SDK adapters</h2>
    <p>
      These provider packages are imported directly in <code>provider/provider.ts</code>, so they do
      not require a dynamic package install at runtime.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Package</th><th>Factory</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>@ai-sdk/openai</code></td><td><code>createOpenAI</code></td><td>Uses Responses API through custom loader.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@ai-sdk/anthropic</code></td><td><code>createAnthropic</code></td><td>Adds Claude Code and fine-grained streaming beta headers.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@ai-sdk/azure</code></td><td><code>createAzure</code></td><td>Can choose chat or responses URL behavior.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@ai-sdk/google</code></td><td><code>createGoogleGenerativeAI</code></td><td>Google Generative AI provider.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@ai-sdk/google-vertex</code></td><td><code>createVertex</code></td><td>Vertex provider with project/location env handling.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@ai-sdk/google-vertex/anthropic</code></td><td><code>createVertexAnthropic</code></td><td>Anthropic on Vertex.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@ai-sdk/openai-compatible</code></td><td><code>createOpenAICompatible</code></td><td>Default fallback for compatible providers.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@openrouter/ai-sdk-provider</code></td><td><code>createOpenRouter</code></td><td>OpenRouter native adapter.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@ai-sdk/xai</code></td><td><code>createXai</code></td><td>xAI adapter.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock</code></td><td><code>createAmazonBedrock</code></td><td>Credential chain, bearer token, region prefix logic.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@ai-sdk/gateway</code></td><td><code>createGateway</code></td><td>AI Gateway package support.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@ai-sdk/vercel</code></td><td><code>createVercel</code></td><td>Vercel AI Gateway package support.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@gitlab/gitlab-ai-provider</code></td><td><code>createGitLab</code></td><td>Uses OAuth/API/env token resolution.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@ai-sdk/github-copilot</code></td><td>Copilot compatibility factory</td><td>Switches between chat and responses for GPT-5 family models.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="dynamic" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Dynamic providers</h2>
    <p>
      nikcli also creates providers that are not just copied from <code>models.dev</code>.
      The two important dynamic loaders are local Ollama and nikcli Inference Gateway.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Detection</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>ollama</code></td><td>Configured <code>provider.ollama.options.baseURL</code>, <code>OLLAMA_BASE_URL</code>, or local <code>127.0.0.1:11434</code> probe.</td><td>Builds OpenAI-compatible models from <code>/models</code> with conservative limits.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli-inference</code></td><td><code>NIKCLI_INFERENCE_URL</code>, <code>NIKCLI_INFERENCE_KEY</code>, or config options.</td><td>Builds models from gateway <code>/models</code>, with pricing, context, thinking, and image input metadata.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Unknown configured provider</td><td>Entry exists in <code>config.provider</code> or has a key.</td><td>Creates a default provider record so custom compatible endpoints can appear.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Plugin provider</td><td>Plugin exposes auth or model hooks.</td><td>Merges options and model lists into the provider catalog.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="auth" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Auth and credentials</h2>
    <p>
      Provider credentials can come from three places: environment variables read from model metadata
      and provider-specific loaders, saved auth records from <code>Auth.Service</code>, or explicit
      config options.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="bash">
export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
export OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
export AWS_REGION=us-east-1
export AWS_PROFILE=default
export NIKCLI_INFERENCE_KEY=nik-...
    </DocCode>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Provider family</th><th>Special handling</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Amazon Bedrock</td><td>Config region wins over <code>AWS_REGION</code>, bearer token can override credential chain, endpoint/baseURL can override endpoint.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Azure</td><td>Can use resource-name derived base URL and switch completion URLs through options.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>GitLab</td><td>Uses saved OAuth, saved API key, or <code>GITLAB_TOKEN</code>; instance URL defaults to <code>https://gitlab.com</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cloudflare</td><td>Uses account/gateway env plus token and transforms auth/header behavior for AI Gateway.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>GitHub Copilot</td><td>Built-in auth plugin can register personal or enterprise Copilot providers.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="models" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Model selection</h2>
    <p>
      The active model is a <code>provider/model</code> string. It can come from CLI flags,
      session/TUI selection, config <code>model</code>, or defaults chosen by provider availability.
      <code>small_model</code> is used for supporting tasks such as title generation.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Used for</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>model</code></td><td>Default primary model for agent turns.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>small_model</code></td><td>Low-cost helper work such as title and summaries.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_MODELS</code></td><td>Keeps alpha models in the catalog.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_MODELS_FETCH</code></td><td>Disables models.dev fetch path where supported.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>provider.*.whitelist</code></td><td>Provider-local model allow-list.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>provider.*.blacklist</code></td><td>Provider-local model block-list.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCallout type="warn" title="Provider/model ids are exact">
      <p>
        <code>Provider.ModelNotFoundError</code> includes provider id, model id, and suggestions.
        Check both sides of the slash before assuming the provider is unavailable.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="runtime" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Runtime streaming</h2>
    <p>
      Runtime ownership starts in <code>session/llm.ts</code>. It builds headers, normalizes messages,
      converts tools, applies <code>ProviderTransform</code>, and streams output. A native runtime in
      <code>session/llm/native-runtime.ts</code> can use <code>@nikcli-ai/llm</code> for OpenAI,
      Anthropic, and OpenAI-compatible providers when requirements are met.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Source</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Message repair</td><td><code>LLM.normalizeStreamMessages</code></td><td>Repairs UI-shaped messages that would otherwise trigger invalid prompt errors.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Headers</td><td><code>buildRequestHeaders</code></td><td>Adds nikcli request headers for nikcli providers and user agent for most others.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Provider options</td><td><code>ProviderTransform.providerOptions</code></td><td>Transforms model/provider options before SDK/native call.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Native runtime</td><td><code>native-runtime.ts</code></td><td>Requires supported provider family and configured API key.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>AI SDK fallback</td><td><code>session/llm/ai-sdk.ts</code></td><td>General runtime path for all supported SDK adapters.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="media" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Images and speech</h2>
    <p>
      Image generation and speech use separate config sections so they can choose different providers
      and models from chat. The tool implementations also read provider-specific environment
      variables for OpenRouter and ElevenLabs.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="json" title="nikcli.json">
&#123;
  "image": &#123;
    "provider": "openrouter",
    "model": "openai/gpt-5-image"
  &#125;,
  "speak": &#123;
    "provider": "elevenlabs",
    "model": "voice-id",
    "modelId": "eleven_v3",
    "outputFormat": "mp3_44100_128"
  &#125;
&#125;
    </DocCode>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Env</th><th>Used by</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_OPENROUTER_API_KEY</code> / <code>OPENROUTER_API_KEY</code></td><td>OpenRouter image, speech, and voice-related tools.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_ELEVENLABS_API_KEY</code> / <code>ELEVENLABS_API_KEY</code></td><td>ElevenLabs speech provider.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_OPENROUTER_BASE_URL</code></td><td>OpenRouter-compatible base URL override.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_ELEVENLABS_BASE_URL</code></td><td>ElevenLabs base URL override.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="refresh" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Refresh and cache</h2>
    <p>
      Provider service state is cached per instance. After writes that change auth or
      <code>config.provider.*</code>, route handlers call provider refresh so subsequent list and
      language-model reads see the new credentials and options.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Mutation</th><th>Refresh path</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Save provider API key</td><td><code>server/httpapi/provider.ts</code> or <code>httpapi/provider.ts</code> writes auth and refreshes provider cache.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Remove provider auth</td><td>Auth removal clears the saved record and refreshes.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Config provider update</td><td>Config route update invalidates provider state through route helper.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Plugin auth loader change</td><td>Provider service rebuilds plugin-derived options during refresh.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="failure-modes" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Failure modes</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>Check</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Provider absent from model list</td><td>Filtered by <code>enabled_providers</code>/<code>disabled_providers</code>, missing auth, or failed dynamic probe.</td><td>Inspect config filters and provider log entries.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Model id missing</td><td>Alpha/deprecated filtering, provider allow/block list, or no API key for paid nikcli models.</td><td>Enable experimental models only if the model status requires it.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Bedrock authentication failure</td><td>Region/profile/bearer token mismatch.</td><td>Check config region, <code>AWS_REGION</code>, <code>AWS_PROFILE</code>, bearer token, and endpoint.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>OpenAI-compatible usage missing</td><td>Provider options disabled usage inclusion or compatible endpoint omits usage.</td><td>Check <code>includeUsage</code> and provider response.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Invalid prompt error</td><td>Malformed message shape reached runtime.</td><td>Verify <code>normalizeStreamMessages</code> input and message history.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Fresh key not used</td><td>Provider cache was not refreshed after auth/config write.</td><td>Call provider refresh or use route handlers that already do it.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="source-anchors" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Source anchors</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Need</th><th>File</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Provider catalog and SDK cache</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/provider/provider.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Provider transforms</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/provider/transform.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Provider auth routes</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/server/httpapi/provider.ts</code>, <code>packages/nikcli/src/server/httpapi/provider.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Session runtime hot path</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/session/llm.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Native runtime</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/session/llm/native-runtime.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>LLM package providers</td><td><code>packages/llm/src/providers</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Image and speech tools</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/tool/generate_image.ts</code>, <code>packages/nikcli/src/tool/speak.ts</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
